WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.701
Welcome, everybody.
Enjoy yourself.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:05.133
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.367
Yeah, you're here. You made it.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:10.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
It is the holiday season.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.934
Isn't it a great time
to be here in New York City?

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.300
Doesn't it feel good?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.133
But I just saw that the police
just warned tourists

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.367
to be on the lookout
for pickpockets.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.467
And to everyone in the audience
who just checked your pockets,

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.501
it's too late now.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:27.000
You can never be too safe.
That's why this time of year,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.434
instead of a wallet,
I keep all my money in crypto.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.267
That's right.
Pickpockets are everywhere.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.868
'Cause nothing ruins a week
of $200 Broadway tickets

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.968
and $12 pretzels
like getting ripped off.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.534
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.267
Hey, here's some good news
for the holidays.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.501
After more than a year
of record inflation,

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.601
it looks like prices
are finally starting to go down.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.601
Yeah. So...

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.267
So, take that, annoying people

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:55.000
who finished all their
Christmas shopping in November.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.400
Ha ha!

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.467
We win!

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.834
Some political news.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.501
Tomorrow is
the Georgia Senate runoff

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.767
between Herschel Walker
and Senator Raphael Warnock.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.567
Warnock's supporters said
that they're voting for him

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.067
because of his policies,
while Walker's supporters say

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.033
they're voting for him
because it's funny.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.267
More than 1.8 million Georgia
residents have already voted,

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.400
and that's just
Herschel Walker's children.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.267
[ Audience oohs ]
Right now --

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:24.834
[ Applause ]
Right now --

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.334
-Whoa!

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.467
-Right now,
Warnock is leading Walker

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.567
in the polls by about 4 points.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.400
Yeah, only 4 points.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.167
That explains
Warnock's slogan...

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.767
It's like -- It's only 4 points.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.167
Tomorrow is the big runoff

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.868
between Herschel Walker
and Raphael Warnock.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.033
And I must say,
it's nice to see two candidates

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.467
set aside their personal attacks

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.467
and focus on real issues
in their campaign.

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.467
Check out this ad
for Herschel Walker.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.167
-Herschel Walker
has always let Georgians know

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.400
where he stands
on the important issues

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.100
like taxes, jobs...

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.367
and vampires.
-[ Hissing ]

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.567
-I don't know if you know.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.200
Vampires are some cool people,
are they not?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.167
But I'm-a tell you something
today I found out.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.734
A werewolf can kill a vampire.
Do you know that?

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.300
-Where does Raphael Warnock
stand on vampires?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.667
He's never told us.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:11.701
But Herschel Walker has.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.100
-Because, you know,
gotta have a stake

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.334
and gotta have a thing
that kill 'em in the heart.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.734
And you got a necklace of
garlic, 'cause that work.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.300
I don't know what it does,
but it work.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.601
Gotta have a cross 'cause
it burns. I know that works.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.801
-So I don't want to be
a vampire anymore.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:28.934
I want to be a werewolf.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.033
[ Wolf howls ]

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.467
-Well, everyone's
talking about this.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.067
Over the weekend,
former President Trump

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:42.667
called for the 2020 election
to be overturned

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.634
by terminating the Constitution.

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.067
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.133
And Trump can actually do it
because he has the real

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:50.367
Constitution hanging in
the bathroom at Mar-a-Lago.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.234
[ Laughter ]
So he could...

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.300
Trump wants to terminate
the Constitution.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.067
Then a staffer held a brick
to his ear like,

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.501
"Yeah, working on it
right now, sir. Yeah."

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.033
Well, listen to this.
I read that compared

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:04.100
to past presidents,
books about President Biden

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.534
aren't selling many copies.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:09.100
Yeah, you can tell that Biden
books aren't that exciting.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.567
I mean, just look
at the blurbs on the back.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.767
For instance, this critic from
"The New York Times" wrote...

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.801
Next up,
"The Washington Post" wrote...

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.968
Then "USA Today" wrote...

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Wow!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.534
-These are the blurbs
on the back of --

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:34.067
-These are the blurbs
on the back of the book

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.734
that real humans wrote. Wow.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.200
"Time" Magazine wrote...

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.467
And finally,
the "Chicago Tribune" wrote...

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.200
I mean, why would you put that
on the back of the --

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.234
-Wow.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.701
[ Applause ]

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:53.067
-Some entertainment news.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.367
A new episode of "White Lotus"
dropped last night,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.934
and it was a real doozy.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.968
-Oh, no. No spoilers.
I haven't seen it yet.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.734
-Oh, I wasn't
gonna spoil anything.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.067
I was just saying
it was a good episode. I --

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:03.667
-I don't care.
I might be able

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:07.000
